Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Differentiate implicitly and collect the derivative terms:

$$
\begin{aligned}
4 x - 6+\left(6 y + 2\right)\frac{dy}{dx}&=0 \\
\left(6 y + 2\right)\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\left(4 x - 6\right) \\
\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\frac{4 x - 6}{6 y + 2}
\end{aligned}
$$

Evaluate the tangent slope at the given point:

$$
m_{\mathrm{t}}=-\frac{-10}{-4}=- \frac{5}{2}
$$

The tangent line uses $m=- \frac{5}{2}$.

Use the given point and this slope:

$$
\begin{aligned}
y-\left(-1\right)&=- \frac{5}{2}\left(x-\left(-1\right)\right) \\
y&=- \frac{5}{2}\left(x-\left(-1\right)\right)+\left(-1\right)
\end{aligned}
$$

At the $x$-axis, $y=0$. Substitute and simplify:

$$
\begin{aligned}
0&=- \frac{5}{2}\left(x-\left(-1\right)\right)+\left(-1\right) \\
x-\left(-1\right)&=-\frac{-1}{- \frac{5}{2}} \\
x&=- \frac{7}{5}
\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore $P=\left(- \frac{7}{5},0\right)$.
